# Build context is the repo root (compose builds every service with `context: .`).
# Exclude host-generated, architecture-specific artifacts so a `COPY <dir> ./`
# in a Dockerfile can never clobber the deps installed inside the image
# (e.g. an arm64 host node_modules/.venv overwriting the linux-x64 install and
# breaking `tsc`/native binaries). Keeps the context small too.
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/dist
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

.git
data
backups
*.tar.gz

# The acceptance suite's per-run scratch: its own data dir (recorded bags —
# hundreds of MB after a few runs), plus Playwright's traces and videos. No
# image copies any of it, and leaving it in the context makes every service
# build pay for the last E2E run.
e2e/.run
e2e/test-results
e2e/playwright-report
